I hope I haven't started a big discussion, most of which will be =
irrelevant
to development of LaTeX 3, about "theses, double-spacing, is =
suthesis.sty
obsolete? etc."

I've just send an item off to TeXhax on this subject.  I'd suggest that
anyone wishing to air views waits until my entry appears in TeXhax, and =
then
responds IN TEXHAX.

After a while it may be apparent whether/not there has been
general progress in getting regulations changed and/or that suthesis.sty
etc.  are/aren't obsolete.  Thus Frank may get to know whether =
suthesis.sty
is/isn't the sort of archived thing that is worth converting (but daily
messages on LATEX-L about theses, double-spacing, etc., will be =
avoided).

                                                                      =
David


